# bruhswer — files that must never reach a public repository.
#
# Patterns here are deliberately SPECIFIC. A broad rule like `*.key` or `tools/` is
# how source files go missing without anyone noticing, and a security tool whose
# repository silently omits part of itself cannot be audited. Every entry below either
# names an exact artefact or is anchored to a directory that contains no source.

# --- secrets and credentials -----------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
secrets.json
*.credentials

# Private keys, WITHOUT swallowing source. `*.key` alone would also match a legitimate
# file such as `signing.key.md` or a fixture named `test.key`; anchoring to the
# extension and listing the real cases keeps the rule honest.
*.private.key
*.secret.key

# --- bruhswer runtime state ------------------------------------------------------
# All of this normally lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\BRUHWSER, outside the repository.
# These patterns are belt-and-braces for anyone who redirects it here.
#
# EVERY ONE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not stylistic.
# An unanchored `downloads/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth - which
# includes bruhswer/app/downloads/, a SOURCE package containing quarantine.py. The
# unanchored version of this list would have silently published a repository with
# the entire download-quarantine module missing, and the app would not have
# imported. Caught by an independent review before publication; anchor these.
/BRUHWSER/
/profiles/
/quarantine/
/state/
/logs/
/downloads/
*.log

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# __pycache__ and bytecode are safe unanchored: no source directory is ever named
# that. Everything below which names a plausible package directory IS anchored,
# for the reason given above.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/
.Python
/build/
/dist/
/sdist/
/wheels/
/develop-eggs/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# --- test and tooling caches -----------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- IDE and editor --------------------------------------------------------------
# .idea holds absolute paths to the developer's machine and their run configurations.
# bruhswer must run without PyCharm (brief §38), so none of this belongs in the repo.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- installer build output ------------------------------------------------------
# The .iss SOURCE is committed and reviewable. Only compiled output is excluded, so
# nobody can quietly ship an installer whose script is not in the repository.
installer/Output/
installer/build/
*.exe
!installer/**/*.iss

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# --- local machine artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
*.local
local.settings.json
/scratch/
/tmp/
